[00:01.03]易考范文二十四
[00:03.44]In the interesting drawing,
[00:07.27]a beautifully-dressed woman is standing there,
[00:10.00]a piece of red cloth covering her face.
[00:13.72]However, when a man lifts the cloth, he is shocked to see an ugly face.
[00:18.97]A word—advertisement—stands out on the cloth.
[00:22.69]Obviously, the purpose of the drawing is to appeal to the public
[00:26.95]for more concern about false advertising.
[00:29.80]Now, we live in a world of advertisements,
[00:33.19]which appear on mass media such as TV, radio, newspaper and magazine.
[00:38.77]Usually, advertisers make a point of fine pictures, melodious music or charming stars,
[00:46.31]which, in some cases, are merely a deceitful veil on fake merchandize.
[00:51.34]Moreover, some advertisers boast about the effectiveness of the products,
[00:57.14]but consumers sometimes are disappointed to find the products are not so good.
[01:03.05]To solve the problem, my suggestions are as follows.
[01:07.31]First, it is essential for consumers to use their reason to discern the authenticity of the ads.
[01:14.97]In addition, advertisers should increase their awareness of public responsibility
[01:20.66]to ensure the truthfulness of the ads they design.
[01:24.05]At the same time, the media must ban ads as soon as they are found to be misleading and exaggerating.
[01:31.16]Of course, we cannot solely rely on the morality of advertisers and the media,
[01:36.51]because stronger supervision,
[01:38.38]stricter laws and regulations play a more important role in eliminating deceptive advertisements.


